<title>ITALY: Italy's Berlusconi criticises ERM re-entry rate.</title>
<headline>Italy's Berlusconi criticises ERM re-entry rate.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-11-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Right-wing leader Silvio Berlusconi said on Sunday that a European Union agreement for the lira to return to the Exchange Rate Mechanism at 990 lire to the mark was not good for Italian industry.</p>
<p>&quot;It is not a favourable rate,&quot; Berlusconi told reporters while attending a football match in Milan. &quot;I thought Italian industry deserved a better rate.&quot;</p>
<p>Asked if Italy had any alternative to rejoining the currency grid, Berlusconi said: &quot;It was a move which had to be made, it would have been better to have obtained a better rate.&quot;</p>
<p>Berlusconi, who served as Prime Minister for seven months in 1994, is leader of the right-wing Freedom Alliance.</p>
<p>Berlusconi had called for a weaker central parity rate for the lira of 1,050 lire against the mark.</p>
</text>
